{"name":"Eleanor Ann","hex":"#40373e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ann","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Obolo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An annate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ann"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eleanor","blocks":[{"text":"Eleanor is a feminine given name, originally from an Old French adaptation of the Old Provençal name Aliénor. It was the name of a number of women of royalty and nobility in western Europe during the High Middle Ages. The name was introduced to England by Eleanor of Aquitaine, who came to marry King Henry II. It was also borne by Eleanor of Provence, who became queen consort of England as the wife of King Henry III, and Eleanor of Castile, wife of Edward I."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/EleanordeProvence.jpg/330px-EleanordeProvence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor"},{"title":"Anne","blocks":[{"text":"Anne, alternatively spelled Ann, is a form of the Latin female name Anna. This in turn is a representation of the Hebrew Hannah, which means 'favour' or 'grace'. Related names include Annie and Ana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/330px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/500px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/1280px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/500px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnne1705.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}